# Swan Compiler 2 — Driver
# Swift-inspired compilation coordinator.
#
# The driver owns command-line parsing, source-file loading, target selection,
# diagnostics, build modes, output paths, and stage scheduling.
# It MUST NOT contain lexer, parser, semantic-analysis, optimizer, or backend
# implementation logic.
#
# Required pipeline:
# source -> lexer -> parser -> AST -> sema -> SILGen -> SIL verification
# -> SIL demand analysis -> SIL optimization -> IRGen -> SVM generation
# -> SVM verification -> SVM optimization -> target lowering -> codegen
# -> object emission -> linker.
#
# Build modes:
# - parse: stop after AST construction and validation.
# - typecheck: stop after semantic analysis.
# - emit-sil: stop after verified, optimized SIL.
# - emit-svm: stop after verified, optimized SVM.
# - emit-asm: stop after target code generation.
# - emit-object: stop after object emission.
# - build: emit and link the final artifact.
#
# Invariant: a failed stage prevents every later stage from running.
# Invariant: diagnostics retain source file, byte range, line, and column.
# Invariant: target selection is explicit and independent of SVM generation.
# Invariant: unsupported language features or target operations are errors.
#
# Implementation status: orchestration contract; stage execution is not yet
# wired. Compiler 1 remains the executable bootstrap until stage parity exists.
